---
title: Spinach Artichoke Dip
servings: 8
prepTime: 5 minutes
cookTime: 25 minutes
totalTime: 30 min
difficulty: Easy
Rating: 10/10
description: Differs slightly from printed version. This recipe adds 1/4 cup sour cream and omitted the 1 1/2 tsp Worcestershire sauce (added to ingredients). This recipe has 1.5 cups mozzarella, the printed recipe only uses 1/4 cup.
source: https://www.mantitlement.com/skillet-spinach-artichoke-dip/
tags: Appetizer
---

= Prepare Dip =
Defrost, squeeze dry, and chop the @spinach{10%ounces}(frozen).

In a #large bowl{}, combine the spinach, @artichoke hearts{14%ounce}(drained and chopped), @mayonnaise{1/4%cup}, 
@sour cream{1/4%cup}, @cream cheese{8%ounces}(at room temperature), @grated parmesan cheese{1/2%cup},
@garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, @black pepper{1/2%tsp}, @cayenne pepper{1/4%tsp},
@ground nutmeg{1/4%tsp}, @Worcestershire sauce{1.5%teaspoons}, and @mozzarella cheese{1%cup}.
Mix well to combine.

= Oven Instructions =
Preheat the oven to 375°F.

Pour the filling into an #oven proof skillet{} or an #8″x8″ baking dish{}.
Top with additional @mozzarella cheese{1/2%cup} and @grated parmesan cheese{2%tbsp}.

Bake for ~{25%minutes} until the filling is bubbling and the cheese is melted on top.

Place under the broiler for 3-4 minutes if you want to the top browned, or serve as is.

= Slow Cooker Instructions =
Pour the filling into a 2-3 quart #slow cooker{} that's been sprayed with non-stick cooking spray.
Cook on low heat for 2 hours or until the filling is warmed through.

Once the dip is warm, add an additional @mozzarella cheese{1/2%cup} and @grated parmesan cheese{2%tbsp}
 to the top of the dip, cover for a few minutes to let the cheese melt and then serve.
 Use the warm setting on your slow cooker to keep the dip warm.

